Candidate A/control direct custom ratios are
0.959860/0.958225/0.965809/0.958208/0.978596 (geomean 0.964109, 3.72%
speedup).  Normalizing each custom result by its paired Humming window gives
0.957308/0.958331/0.957314/0.950732/0.988140 (geomean 0.962276, 3.92%
speedup).  Candidate B repeats and strengthens every point: direct geomean
0.956472 (4.55% speedup), paired-normalized geomean 0.949088 (5.36%).

Decision: accept offline normalization as the new winner.  It converts the
earlier scale-synthesis diagnostic into a full-checkpoint-capable, branch-free
runtime path and gives repeatable W13, W2 and end-to-end gains.  Candidate A
versus the immediately adjacent control is the conservative causal estimate;
Candidate B is confirmation, not the headline delta.
